Martin Read schrieb:
> 
> byron@cc.gatech.edu (Byron A Jeff) wrote:
> >Well you can. And every class, even the wombats, should take advantage of
> >it.

'Should' is a big statement. It may be that every class can profit
from the protection racket, but i find that everybody can do just as
well _not_ doing it. 

> OTOH, it's close to the least bad plan for a healer (who starts with an
> enormous pile of MONEY, some healing potions, a wand suitable for evading
> enemies with, and very little else of note), and reasonable for an
> archaeologist or tourist.

I don't know - my healers seem to have a survival rate (chance of
making it to the castle in one piece) between 1/3 and 1/2 without ever
bothering with the racket. I don't know what typical success rates on
the racket are (note that succeeding with the racket does not equal
reaching the castle), and i like to explore levels too much to go to
the trouble of teaching myself the racket.

> >1) Let you pet be your protector.
> 
> Also, be careful with your pet when you get to minetown; it might just
> decide it fancies some tasty watch captain meat, and the watch captain
> has a *much* better AC than it does.

I think what makes the captain such a problem is not the AC but
damage: a cat or dog can be expected to take about ten hits to kill a
watch captain [1], a watch captain kills a max level fully healed
large cat with six average-strength blows; a cat/dog attacks once per
round, a watch captain twice per round.

[1] that's an average hitdie rolls, minimum-level watch captain. To
kill a maxed-out watch captain, a large cat/dog would need 24
average-power attacks.

> Indeed.  Be prepared for the possibility that the minetown will be at a
> depth of 10 (mine entrance on 5, minetown on 5th level of mines);

At least for normal NetHack, i'm almost certain that minetown will not
be below lvl 8 (afaik deepest possible mine entrance is lvl 4, and
minetown is either on level 3 or 4 of the mines).

> (I'm trying to remember whether orcs of various
> sorts acn get generated in the mines;

They can. I'm only aware of Uruk-Hai being generated with bows (and
poisoned arrows), not Mordor-orcs.

